        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: American Samoa, Native American tribal lands, United States\n- People: Edith \"Edie\" Windsor\n- Events: the Windsor case, same-sex marriage recognition\n\nFacts:\n- Edith \"Edie\" Windsor was the main plaintiff in the Windsor case.\n- After the Windsor case, some areas of the United States were still able to deny same-sex marriages.\n- American Samoa was one of the United States areas that could still deny same-sex marriages after the Windsor case.\n- Not all Native American tribal lands could deny same-sex marriages after the Windsor case.",
